      "side": 1,
      "message": "Misleading inline comment for Operator privilege row\n\nIssue: The comment says the Operator user is \"able to delete IP address\", but the corresponding template data row at line 587 passes [${HTTP_FORBIDDEN}] as the expected status code, meaning the test expects the delete to be denied. This is a copy-paste error from the Administrator row comment. The mismatch will confuse anyone reading the test and could mask a real privilege regression (an incorrect pass when Operator should be allowed to delete).\n\nFix:\n```\n    # Verify LDAP user with Operator privilege is forbidden to delete IP address.\n```\n\nWhy: Accurate comments are critical in RBAC/privilege tests. A mismatched comment creates ambiguity about the intended access-control policy and makes regression failures harder to diagnose.",
